{"title":"Career Roadmap · Pharmacovigilance Executive","role":"Pharmacovigilance Executive","summary":"A Pharmacovigilance (PV) Executive is responsible for detecting, documenting, assessing, processing, and reporting information related to adverse drug reactions (ADRs) and adverse events (AEs) to help ensure medicines remain safe throughout their lifecycle.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Pharm (Bachelor of Pharmacy)","Course":"Pharmacology / Clinical Research"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Pharmacovigilance (PV) Executive is responsible for detecting, documenting, assessing, processing, and reporting information related to adverse drug reactions (ADRs) and adverse events (AEs) to help ensure medicines remain safe throughout their lifecycle."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Pharm student specializing in Pharmacology / Clinical Research, this is one of the more directly aligned entry-level careers."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR) processing"},{"text":"Adverse event identification and case intake"},{"text":"Case triage and data entry"},{"text":"Seriousness and expectedness assessment"},{"text":"MedDRA coding"},{"text":"Causality assessment support"},{"text":"Follow-up with healthcare professionals/patients"},{"text":"Literature surveillance"},{"text":"Safety database management"},{"text":"Aggregate safety reporting support"},{"text":"Signal detection support"},{"text":"Regulatory compliance and documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Pharm can provide a strong entry route into operational PV roles. More advanced positions in signal management, benefit-risk assessment, safety science, epidemiology, or PV leadership may require postgraduate study and/or substantial experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Undergraduate / Entry Preparation"},{"text":"Pharmacology, clinical research, ADRs, clinical trials, medical terminology, PV fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"PV Executive → Senior PV Associate"},{"text":"ICSR processing, MedDRA, safety databases, QC, literature surveillance"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"PV Specialist / Safety Scientist"},{"text":"Signal detection, aggregate reports, risk management, benefit-risk assessment"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"PV Manager / Safety Lead"},{"text":"Global PV operations, regulatory strategy, governance, safety systems"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Pharm","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Pharmaceutical & Biological Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy and physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical chemistry"},{"text":"Basic pharmacology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Basic statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Drug","Target","Pharmacological effect","Therapeutic effect","Adverse effect"]},{"type":"p","text":"Also learn the difference between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Side effect"},{"text":"Adverse event"},{"text":"Adverse drug reaction"},{"text":"Medication error"},{"text":"Drug interaction"},{"text":"Overdose"},{"text":"Lack of efficacy"},{"text":"Product quality complaint"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Pharmacology Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop deeper knowledge of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmacokinetics"},{"text":"Pharmacodynamics"},{"text":"Receptor pharmacology"},{"text":"Dose-response relationships"},{"text":"Drug toxicity"},{"text":"Drug interactions"},{"text":"Contraindications"},{"text":"Drug safety"},{"text":"Therapeutic index"},{"text":"Organ-system pharmacology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"High-value therapeutic areas"},{"type":"p","text":"Study common safety profiles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiovascular drugs"},{"text":"CNS drugs"},{"text":"Anti-infectives"},{"text":"Oncology drugs"},{"text":"Antidiabetics"},{"text":"Respiratory drugs"},{"text":"Gastrointestinal drugs"},{"text":"Immunological therapies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A PV professional should be able to understand what happened to the patient and whether the drug could plausibly be involved."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Clinical Research + Pharmacovigilance"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important phase for career specialization."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trial phases"},{"text":"Clinical trial protocols"},{"text":"Investigator responsibilities"},{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Clinical trial documentation"},{"text":"Safety reporting"},{"text":"Serious adverse events"},{"text":"Clinical trial databases"},{"text":"Good Clinical Practice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacovigilance"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICSR lifecycle"},{"text":"Case intake"},{"text":"Case validation"},{"text":"Case triage"},{"text":"Case processing"},{"text":"Follow-up"},{"text":"Medical review"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Case narratives"},{"text":"Literature monitoring"},{"text":"Signal detection"},{"text":"Aggregate safety reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 / Final Stage — Job-Ready PV Professional"},{"type":"p","text":"Build practical competence in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MedDRA terminology"},{"text":"WHO Drug / drug dictionaries"},{"text":"Safety databases"},{"text":"Case processing workflows"},{"text":"Medical coding"},{"text":"Seriousness assessment"},{"text":"Expectedness"},{"text":"Causality"},{"text":"Regulatory timelines"},{"text":"Clinical safety documentation"},{"text":"Literature surveillance"},{"text":"Quality management"},{"text":"Excel-based PV analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"If the B.Pharm program is structured as a 4-year degree, use the final year heavily for PV internships, clinical research exposure, case-processing practice and a capstone project."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Pharmacovigilance Knowledge"}]},{"heading":"ICSR Processing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the complete workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Adverse Event Received","Case Intake","Case Validation","Duplicate Check","Seriousness Assessment","Data Entry","Medical Coding","Causality / Expectedness","Narrative Preparation","Medical Review","Quality Control","Regulatory Submission / Archiving"]}]},{"heading":"MedDRA","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"MedDRA — Medical Dictionary for Regulatory Activities is a critical terminology system in pharmacovigilance."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn its hierarchy:"},{"type":"flow","items":["System Organ Class","High Level Group Term","High Level Term","Preferred Term","Lowest Level Term"]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice converting clinical descriptions into appropriate standardized terminology."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Patient reports \"severe headache after taking medicine.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how this type of reported information can be represented using standardized medical terminology."}]},{"heading":"Seriousness vs Severity","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This distinction is extremely important."},{"type":"h","text":"Severity"},{"type":"p","text":"Describes how intense an event is."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mild"},{"text":"Moderate"},{"text":"Severe"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Seriousness"},{"type":"p","text":"Determines whether the event meets regulatory seriousness criteria."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples can include events involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Death"},{"text":"Life-threatening circumstances"},{"text":"Hospitalization"},{"text":"Significant disability"},{"text":"Congenital anomaly"},{"text":"Other medically important conditions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong PV candidate should never treat \"severe\" and \"serious\" as interchangeable terms."}]},{"heading":"Causality Assessment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to evaluate whether there is a reasonable possibility that the drug contributed to an event."},{"type":"p","text":"Consider:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Temporal relationship"},{"text":"Dechallenge"},{"text":"Rechallenge"},{"text":"Alternative causes"},{"text":"Biological plausibility"},{"text":"Existing safety information"},{"text":"Patient history"}]}]},{"heading":"Expectedness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand whether an adverse event is consistent with the known safety information for the medicinal product."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to work with documents such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reference safety information"},{"text":"Product information"},{"text":"Investigator's brochure"},{"text":"Core safety information"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Research Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"A PV Executive should understand the clinical research ecosystem."},{"type":"flow","items":["Preclinical Research","Phase I","Phase II","Phase III","Regulatory Approval","Phase IV / Post-Marketing Surveillance","Continuous Pharmacovigilance"]},{"type":"p","text":"This helps the professional understand how safety information evolves throughout a drug's lifecycle."},{"type":"h","text":"Tools & Software Skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"table","header":["Tool","Purpose"],"rows":[[{"text":"MS Excel"},{"text":"Case tracking, reconciliation, analysis"}],[{"text":"Word"},{"text":"Narratives and documentation"}],[{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Safety presentations"}],[{"text":"MedDRA"},{"text":"Medical coding"}],[{"text":"Safety databases"},{"text":"ICSR processing"}],[{"text":"Clinical trial systems"},{"text":"Clinical safety data"}],[{"text":"Literature databases"},{"text":"Safety surveillance"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Excel skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Become comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"VLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"IF"},{"text":"COUNTIF/COUNTIFS"},{"text":"SUMIF/SUMIFS"},{"text":"Pivot Tables"},{"text":"Filters"},{"text":"Conditional formatting"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Power Query"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data & Analytics Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern pharmacovigilance increasingly benefits from data analytics."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Percentages"},{"text":"Rates"},{"text":"Frequencies"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Basic epidemiological concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Optional advanced skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Basic machine learning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A PV professional does not need to become a full-time software engineer, but analytical capability can create a significant advantage."},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio Projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build projects that demonstrate actual PV understanding."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — ADR Case Processing Simulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a fictional dataset containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient information"},{"text":"Suspected drug"},{"text":"Event"},{"text":"Date of administration"},{"text":"Event onset"},{"text":"Outcome"},{"text":"Medical history"},{"text":"Concomitant medications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then create a simulated PV workflow."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — MedDRA Coding Exercise"},{"type":"p","text":"Create 50–100 fictional patient event descriptions."},{"type":"p","text":"Map:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Report","Clinical Interpretation","Standardized Term","MedDRA Coding"]},{"type":"p","text":"Document your reasoning."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Pharmacovigilance Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Use Excel or Power BI to build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cases by month"},{"text":"Cases by therapeutic area"},{"text":"Serious vs non-serious cases"},{"text":"Events by organ system"},{"text":"Outcome distribution"},{"text":"Suspected medicines"},{"text":"Source of reports"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates a strong portfolio artifact."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Literature Surveillance Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Select a fictional or publicly documented medicine and demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature search strategy"},{"text":"Identification of potential safety information"},{"text":"Screening"},{"text":"Relevance assessment"},{"text":"Case identification"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Drug Safety Signal Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a synthetic dataset and investigate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Drug","Adverse Event","Frequency","Pattern","Potential Signal","Further Evaluation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Clearly label the dataset as synthetic rather than presenting the findings as real regulatory evidence."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target internships in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical Companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmacovigilance"},{"text":"Drug safety"},{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"Clinical data management"},{"text":"Medical affairs"},{"text":"Regulatory affairs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CROs"},{"type":"p","text":"Particularly valuable for gaining exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICSR processing"},{"text":"Clinical trials"},{"text":"Safety databases"},{"text":"Literature surveillance"},{"text":"Client projects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other relevant environments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical research organizations"},{"text":"Drug safety service providers"},{"text":"Hospitals with clinical research units"},{"text":"Academic pharmacology/clinical research groups"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Pharm Year 2","Clinical Research Exposure","B.Pharm Year 3","PV / Drug Safety Internship","Final Year","PV Project + Industry Internship","PV Executive / PV Associate"]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A B.Pharm graduate with the right PV preparation can target roles such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmacovigilance Executive"},{"text":"Pharmacovigilance Associate"},{"text":"Drug Safety Associate"},{"text":"Safety Data Associate"},{"text":"ICSR Processing Associate"},{"text":"Clinical Research Associate — entry-level where eligible"},{"text":"Clinical Data Associate"},{"text":"Medical Information Associate"},{"text":"Drug Safety Operations Associate"},{"text":"Regulatory Operations Associate"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact title and eligibility criteria vary by employer."},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Requirement","Priority"],"rows":[[{"text":"B.Pharm / Life Sciences background"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Pharmacology"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Pharmacovigilance fundamentals"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"ICSR processing"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"MedDRA"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"English communication"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Attention to detail"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Regulatory awareness"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Safety database exposure"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"★★★☆☆"}],[{"text":"SQL/Python"},{"text":"★★☆☆☆"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize practical knowledge over collecting certificates."},{"type":"h","text":"High-value areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmacovigilance fundamentals"},{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"GCP"},{"text":"MedDRA"},{"text":"Drug safety case processing"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Regulatory affairs"},{"text":"Clinical data management"},{"text":"Excel/data analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For MedDRA and regulated PV work, use authoritative training/materials where possible rather than relying solely on generic certificate courses."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A postgraduate qualification is not mandatory for every entry-level PV role, but can improve access to specialized positions."},{"type":"h","text":"Strong options"},{"type":"h","text":"M.Pharm"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential specializations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmacology"},{"text":"Pharmacy Practice"},{"text":"Clinical Pharmacy"},{"text":"Regulatory Affairs"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical Analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"M.Sc."},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant fields:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Pharmacology"},{"text":"Toxicology"},{"text":"Life Sciences"},{"text":"Drug Development"},{"text":"Biotechnology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"MBA"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful later for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare management"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical management"},{"text":"Operations"},{"text":"Project management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Ph.D."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for advanced:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drug safety research"},{"text":"Pharmacology"},{"text":"Toxicology"},{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"Safety science"},{"text":"Academic/research careers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"p","text":"After gaining experience, the professional can specialize in:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. ICSR Operations"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case processing"},{"text":"Case quality"},{"text":"Medical coding"},{"text":"Case narratives"},{"text":"Follow-up"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Signal Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Safety signals"},{"text":"Disproportionality concepts"},{"text":"Trend analysis"},{"text":"Literature"},{"text":"Benefit-risk evaluation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Aggregate Reporting"},{"type":"p","text":"Work with safety reports such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Periodic safety reports"},{"text":"Aggregate safety analyses"},{"text":"Risk management documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Literature Surveillance"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scientific literature"},{"text":"Safety case identification"},{"text":"Medical review"},{"text":"Signal identification"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Clinical Trial Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trial adverse events"},{"text":"Serious adverse events"},{"text":"Safety reconciliation"},{"text":"Sponsor/CRO processes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Safety Data Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine PV +:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Data visualization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a particularly strong future-oriented path."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Pharm","PV Intern / Clinical Research Intern","Pharmacovigilance Executive / Associate","Senior PV Associate","PV Specialist","Senior PV Specialist","PV Manager","Senior Manager / Safety Lead","PV Director / Head of Pharmacovigilance"]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative specialist route"},{"type":"flow","items":["PV Associate","Safety Data Specialist","Signal Detection Specialist","Safety Scientist","Senior Safety Scientist","Safety Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"Pharmacovigilance is increasingly becoming a data-intensive and AI-assisted discipline."},{"type":"h","text":"AI-assisted case processing"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case intake automation"},{"text":"Duplicate detection"},{"text":"Data extraction"},{"text":"Medical terminology suggestions"},{"text":"Narrative assistance"},{"text":"Quality checks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"NLP"},{"type":"p","text":"Natural Language Processing can help extract:"},{"type":"p","text":"Patient"},{"type":"p","text":"Drug"},{"type":"p","text":"Event"},{"type":"p","text":"Dose"},{"type":"p","text":"Time"},{"type":"p","text":"Outcome"},{"type":"p","text":"Medical History"},{"type":"p","text":"from unstructured safety reports."},{"type":"h","text":"Machine Learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Signal prioritization"},{"text":"Duplicate detection"},{"text":"Case classification"},{"text":"Literature screening"},{"text":"Safety trend analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Generative AI"},{"type":"p","text":"Future PV professionals should understand how GenAI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Document summarization"},{"text":"Literature screening support"},{"text":"Structured data extraction"},{"text":"Drafting assistance"},{"text":"Knowledge retrieval"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, human medical/regulatory oversight remains essential because PV decisions can have patient-safety and regulatory consequences."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Pharm"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Pharmacology"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical Research"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Pharmacovigilance"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"ICSR Processing"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"MedDRA"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Medical Terminology"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"GCP / Regulatory Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Safety Database Exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Literature Surveillance"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Basic Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Communication & Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Power BI / SQL / Python"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate for Pharmacovigilance Executive should ideally graduate with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Pharm"},{"text":"Strong pharmacology knowledge"},{"text":"Clinical research understanding"},{"text":"Drug safety fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICSR workflow knowledge"},{"text":"MedDRA familiarity"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"ADR/ADE classification"},{"text":"Seriousness assessment"},{"text":"Causality concepts"},{"text":"Literature surveillance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Optional SQL/Python"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"1 relevant internship"},{"text":"2–4 PV/clinical-research projects"},{"text":"Synthetic ICSR processing exercise"},{"text":"MedDRA coding practice"},{"text":"Pharmacovigilance dashboard"},{"text":"Literature surveillance exercise"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong written English"},{"text":"Scientific documentation"},{"text":"Attention to detail"},{"text":"Regulatory discipline"},{"text":"Ability to work with structured workflows"},{"text":"Ability to handle confidential information appropriately"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For ID 2005, the most direct career strategy is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Pharm","Pharmacology + Clinical Research","Pharmacovigilance Fundamentals","MedDRA + ICSR Processing","GCP + Regulatory Knowledge","PV / Clinical Research Internship","Pharmacovigilance Executive / Associate","Senior PV Associate","PV Specialist / Safety Scientist","PV Manager / Safety Lead"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Pharmacology","Pharmacovigilance Operations","MedDRA","Clinical Research","Data Analytics."],"sep":"+","label":"Best future-ready combination"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination keeps the graduate suitable for conventional PV operations while creating a pathway toward signal detection, safety analytics, clinical safety, and AI-assisted pharmacovigilance."}]}]}